>> title: Gumbo
>> category: Soups
>> tags: chicken, sausage, shrimp, okra, creole, one-pot
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: chicken and sausage gumbo, seafood gumbo, gumbo ya-ya, Louisiana gumbo
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — the roux is stirred without stopping, and any way of hurrying it ends in scorched flour and a pot to start again
>> step.1: Thirty-five minutes of flour and oil over medium heat, taken to the colour of milk chocolate.
>> step.2: brown 8 min, out to a plate
>> step.3: stir the roux 35 min, to milk chocolate
>> step.4: sweat the trinity 6 min — the roux stops here
>> step.5: simmer 45 min, shred the chicken in
>> step.6: simmer 8 min, sausage back, filé off the heat
>> step.7: Filé goes in off the heat or the whole pot turns stringy. Rice under it is a second pot and your call.

The roux is made in the gumbo pot, which is the reason this is one pot at all.

Brown @andouille sausage{12%oz}(340 g; sliced in coins) in a #Dutch oven{} for ~brown{8%min}, then out to a plate.

Stir @vegetable oil{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(65 g) over medium heat for ~stir{35%min}, without stopping, until it is the colour of milk chocolate.

Soften @&(~1)dark roux{} with @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @celery{3%ribs}(diced), @green bell pepper{1%large}(diced), @garlic{5%cloves}(minced) for ~saute{6%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)trinity{} with @chicken stock{8%cups}(1.9 L), @bone-in chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(700 g), @bay leaves{2}, @cayenne{1/2%tsp}, @dried thyme{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp} for ~simmer{45%min}, then pull the chicken, shred it and put it back.

Simmer @&(~1)gumbo{} with @&(~4)browned sausage{}, @okra{8%oz}(225 g; sliced), @large shrimp{1%lb}(450 g; peeled), @scallions{4}(sliced), @filé powder{1%tsp}(off the heat) for ~simmer{8%min}.

A bowl of gumbo is dinner as it stands.
